{
  "_doc": "Task enforcement: no code change without a task. Enforced at CHANGE time by a PreToolUse hook, not at commit time. Project-owned and COMMITTED, so the setting binds everyone on the repo rather than living in one machine's .git/hooks. Toggle with: .claude/skills/task-enforce/task-enforce.sh on|off",

  "enabled": false,

  "_enabled_doc": "Set by bin/init at install time. A NEW project (no commits, no tracked files) gets true — there is no mid-stream to disrupt, and defaulting off there means the gate is never turned on at all. An EXISTING project gets false, because a gate that switches itself on mid-stream is a gate people delete; init prints the one-line command to turn it on deliberately. Either way this file is skip-if-exists, so once it exists the setting is yours and no install rewrites it. Toggle with: .claude/skills/task-enforce/task-enforce.sh on|off",

  "classify": {
    "_doc": "Three classes. meta and docs are RECORDED in tasks/CHANGES.md but mint no task; code mints one. audit_anyway overrides both exemptions.",

    "exempt_meta": [
      ".claude/**",
      "tasks/**",
      "deploys/**"
    ],

    "exempt_docs": [
      "docs/**",
      "*.md",
      "LICENSE",
      ".gitignore",
      ".gitattributes",
      ".editorconfig"
    ],

    "audit_anyway": [
      ".claude/environments.json",
      ".claude/env-transport.md",
      "build/environments/*/env.sh",
      "build/environments/*/deploy.sh"
    ],

    "_audit_anyway_doc": "These ship NON-EMPTY on purpose. The exemptions exist so touching a README is not a task — not so the files that define what production IS can be edited untracked. .claude/environments.json holds each environment's class; an agent flipping \"class\": \"prod\" to \"staging\" there would let the next /deploy reach production through a gate working exactly as designed, with no task, no ledger row, and nothing for the commit-time reconciler to catch. Add paths, do not remove these without deciding you are fine with that."
  }
}
